 "short_name": "Elundini",
 "_doc": "Shared ledger layout of this billing system ('TAX INVOICE/STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT', 'CLICK TO PAY OPTIONS' footer): header with Account Number, Account Date, Street/ERF Description and Deposit; a METER READINGS table (meter, type ELECTRICITY/KVA/WATER/TIME OF USE, old and new reading, reading date, reading type, consumption; an older variant prints CONSUMPTION, LEVIED AMOUNT and a READING DATES period instead); an ACCOUNT DETAILS ledger (date, code, description, units, tariff, value, credits with trailing '-'), then undated VAT and INTEREST lines and an ageing row ending in CURRENT and the closing balance. No electricity sub-total is printed, so the electricity total ex VAT is the sum of this municipality's electricity ledger lines: energy lines -> standard kWh/Rand, kVA lines -> demand, basic charge plus electricity credit/debit notes -> other_r. Start/end readings are filled only when exactly one ELECTRICITY meter is printed; total kWh = billed energy units (fallback: summed meter consumption). Fingerprint = the municipality's own printed VAT number + its name. Identity e_ledger_check_r = closing - opening - payments - VAT - interest - every non-electricity ledger line (a ledger closure: it proves every electricity line was captured and parsed, but it is not an electricity figure printed by the bill, because none is). Electricity lines: 'ELECTRICITY UNITS' (standard), 'KVA CHARGES' (demand, 8 of 10), 'ELECTRICITY BASIC CHARGE'; one bill is time-of-use with '<n> PHASE MEDIUM <n> PEAK' / 'OFF PEAK' lines and two TIME OF USE registers, where ELECTRICITY UNITS (third register, same rate as peak) is taken as standard and total kWh = peak + standard + off-peak. Checked on 10 bills: identity 0.00 on 10/10, no contradiction checks.",
